{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover","id":96439,"title":"Is there any hope of a Changeling:tD 20th? Or at least a C:tD/C:tL crossover?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-22T11:30:35-07:00","id":96439,"title":"Is there any hope of a Changeling:tD 20th? Or at least a C:tD/C:tL crossover?","content":"As much as I think Changeling: the Lost was the only line were the New WoD game was better than the old WoD game. I'd still love to see a Changeling 20th Aniversary game and some repairs. The Menehunne, the Spriggans, and so much else were left half-made up. And where was the Sidhe Thallain?<br /> <br /> If a 20th anniversary ed is out, could a crossover between old and new still be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T16:42:14-07:00","id":96585,"title":"","content":"C20 is waiting on Wr20 from what we've been told. But it seems likely as M20 is kicking ass and showing that there's plenty of fan support of these books.<br /> <br /> This means there will, at a minimum, likely by a translation guide for the Changeling games at some point.<br /> <br /> Direct crossover? Unlikely as official product. The translation guides have been the closest we've seen and I haven't heard of an indication of Onyx Path wishing to go further (at least in terms of crossover between the lines level; I think a few of the OP folks would be up for longer translation guides/GMC compatible ones as the games are updated, but I'm not sure that's in the cards from a practicality standpoint).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T15:51:28-07:00","id":97094,"title":"","content":"Probably two years from now. This time next year we will likely be looking at Wraith 20, and then a year from that Changeling 20 if Wraith manages to break out..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T12:34:19-07:00","id":98566,"title":"","content":"If we don't get a C:tD 20th, I will be upset.<br /> <br /> The complete Changeling run still occupies the place of honor on my gaming shelf. It's the only White Wolf game where I haven't felt the need to rewrite huge swaths of factions and history before I actually wanted to play it. It was my first true love in RPGs, and to this day the only game line I had all official products for (Exalted and C:tL come close though). Even though most of my cWoD time was spent in Mage, Changeling was the game I was always thinking about, always doodling sketches of, always writing homebrew for. I have notebooks full of Chimera, custom Arts, Treasures, Freehold maps, charts of the Dreaming where I'd just plop neat looking scribbles with fancy names all over the place, just to have a seed to improvise something later. But surprisingly few homebrew NPCs, because Changeling was the only White Wolf game where I've ever cared to use more than a handful of canon NPCs. Changeling was the only White Wolf game where the metaplot didn't feel like poison to my imagination, partly because it was self-contained, and I almost never had to go to a fucking Vampire book or whatever to find out what was really going on with Changeling, and mostly because it happened on a scale where the PCs could actually contribute to the story, instead of being &quot;rewarded&quot; by being powerless bystanders when the real movers and shakers moved and/or shook.<br /> <br /> I dug W:tO as an artistic statement, but not really as a game. It kind of bums me out to know the possibility of a C:tD20th is gated behind the success of a W:tO20th... but I guess Wraith fans, like Changeling fans, make up for small numbers with tremendous enthusiasm? That's what I'm going to hope for. Because I know a few Changeling fans who will cheerfully bankrupt ourselves all over that Kickstarter, if it ever happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:39:21-07:00","id":98716,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be too worried about the whole &quot;gated behind Wr20&quot; bit. Wr20 was theoretically gated behind M20, but development started on it before M20's Kickstarter even began.<br /> <br /> I think the concern will really be over the initial level responses to whatever the early hints end up being more than how well the Wr20 Kickstarter goes. Though a poor Wr20 Kickstarter could mean a scaled back C20 Kickstarter (and if both don't perform very well, it might mean that we don't see Kickstarters for any 20th books outside the big three after that), that isn't the same as the book never getting made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T03:44:03-07:00","id":99894,"title":"","content":"Wraith and Changeling both have small but fanatically devoted fanbases. So hopefully someone with deep pockets will be part of the eventual KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:35:04-07:00","id":100003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover#post96439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where was the Sidhe Thallain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right there in the open. They called themselves House Balor.<br /> <br /> Well technically they still had a Seelie Legacy but as it is unable to ever be dominant the end result is the same. I always loved this side of 'em. Although I hated their completely unneeded and poorly fitting limit on WP considering how strong willed every Balor NPC seemed to be.<br /> <br /> But yes I too expect C20 to come after Wraith20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:08:27-07:00","id":104862,"title":"","content":"I really don't like Lost and just can't understand folks saying it's a better game than Dreaming. It feels so much more straight jacketing as a setting to me than Dreaming ever did, and the premise makes me never, *ever* want to play a Lost PC.<br /> <br /> I really hope there's a C20, and I really hope that it leaves Changeling: The Lost in Changeling: The Lost. I want it to be the glorious, ultimate version of Changeling: The Dreaming we never got!<br /> <br /> Now, all that being said, I do sometimes mine Lost supplements for my Dreaming games. Goblin Markets is a good resource to steal from for Dreaming, as is Grim Fears. I'd like to see a Changeling Translation Guide to help facilitate that sort of idea mining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:39:52-07:00","id":104887,"title":"","content":"In Changeling the Lost, the characters are, well, changelings. Sad, lonely, lost, broken people. Not necessarily true to the source material (where you just got some time displacement, often with rapid aging consequences), but, essentially, fundamentally humans.<br /> <br /> In Changeling the Dreaming, they are soul-destroying parasites that hollow out people and use them as expendable meat puppets. Hell, to reference the fomori thread, changelings pretty much are fomori, just High Umbra fomori with a bigger spectrum of ick in what they end up as (from happy! happy! joy! all the way to cannibalistic monstrosities).<br /> <br /> I know that's uncharitable, but it's essentially true. It's one of my biggest issues with the game and, when I've run it in the past several decades, I've glossed over it. I've run Lost as well and, besides being darker, grimmer and much more personal, it seemed to hold together better and was more viscerally satisfying than Dreaming. That's with Dreaming games and session both before and after Lost games.<br /> <br /> If the name of the game was Fae the Dreaming, I think I'd be cooler with it. To a degree. Changeling the Dreaming always failed on that one critical point. In all the other games, there was a normal human involved somewhere in the mix: Vampires, Kuei-jin, Mummies, Wraiths were mortal, Mages and Hunters are mortal, Demons wear a meat suit that has a big effect on how their immortal selves can interact with the world, most Werewolves at least thought they were mortals until they changed (I admit the werewolf part is weak, but that has always been my least favorite of the games).<br /> <br /> But the mortal aspect of Changelings is barely addressed. That pretty sidhe princess was someone's little girl and that &quot;noble&quot; spirit inside her just smashed that child's soul, dreams and all and took over her body. And I find that hard to reconcile, because the game wouldn't really be the same if it was dealt with (too much like Vampire or Demon), but that fact it's not dealt with just irritates.<br /> <br /> And, no, I don't have a solution to propose and, even if I did, I would probably want it as a sidebar in C20. Like I said, I don't think the game can really handle that core issue and stay true to what it's supposed to be.<br /> <br /> But Lost really does accomplish something special that Dreaming just doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-03-2014, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:56:20-07:00","id":104901,"title":"","content":"Except it's a merging of souls, not a displacement, that encourages them to new heights neither would probably be able to achieve on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T10:23:01-07:00","id":104911,"title":"","content":"That's one interpretation. Not one that is really explored any more than the other... I've never seen anywhere where an important Prelude scene is the one where the &quot;host&quot; interacts with and is giving a choice about the entry of the &quot;guest&quot;. Much less the Commoners who are born with the soul leech already integrated. No choice allowed. <br /> <br /> It's not a merging if it's not voluntary. And I've seen LOTS about trying to function as a changeling in a banal world, but I've not seen (read as &quot;never seen&quot;) any material on how to deal with your mortal life once you've merged with fae soul. The character just flips over into their new changeling life? So much so that the mortal life is never mentioned. (Obviously this applies only to the sidhe, but they highlight the situation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T10:47:57-07:00","id":104940,"title":"","content":"I always end up looking at CtD as the cWOD game of completely untapped potential. Not that the game is about untapped potential, but that the books absolutely miss so many opportunities to make the game what it could have been. There are so many facets of the game that could be marvelously interesting, and sometimes the game even hints about how that is the case, and then it all gets glossed over to take a backseat between the tug-of-war between &quot;game of escapist fantasy&quot; and &quot;game of the horrors of escapist fantasy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:04:53-07:00","id":104952,"title":"","content":"I agree completely Arms. <br /> <br /> I have to say, I'm not sure I would buy C20. I would definitely look into and see what the buzz was about how they would do it. But, as is, I'd have to think if I would devote any resources more than pdf level max (post-Kickstarter, probably).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T20:56:12-07:00","id":105350,"title":"","content":"Next year, I think we will at least see a &quot;Changeling Translation Guide&quot;.<br /> (Wraith didn't get one, but then again perhaps the concepts between Wraith and Geist just weren't compatible enough to do so?)<br /> <br /> This year at Gen Con, we will find out the fate of Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition. I really hope that C20 happens as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:21:19-07:00","id":105672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=104887#post104887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Changeling the Dreaming, they are soul-destroying parasites that hollow out people and use them as expendable meat puppets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true in the least on so many levels. The Sidhe are the only ones who possess their victims and even they do not destroy these souls but remove them and send them somewhere in the Deep Dreaming, and the Sidhe truly do not see their bodies in any way disposable, they are the Kith most afraid of death as they do not reincarnate and are unsure of their souls ultimate fate. So no expendable meat puppets here.<br /> The commoners have merged their souls with the souls of humanity and are born as such they do not possess their bodies anymore than humans do. It's a single soul within that body, it just happens to be fae touched soul.<br /> <br /> So all in all this point is false.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=104887#post104887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the name of the game was Fae the Dreaming, I think I'd be cooler with it. To a degree. Changeling the Dreaming always failed on that one critical point. In all the other games, there was a normal human involved somewhere in the mix: Vampires, Kuei-jin, Mummies, Wraiths were mortal, Mages and Hunters are mortal, Demons wear a meat suit that has a big effect on how their immortal selves can interact with the world, most Werewolves at least thought they were mortals until they changed (I admit the werewolf part is weak, but that has always been my least favorite of the games).</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling Commoners are just as human as any of the above. They are born humans and for the most part they are humans just like Mages. The difference is that where Mage has an Avatar attached to his soul a Changeling has a Faerie soul attached to his own, in both cases it is this extra quality within their souls that allows them to wield magic and to see into realms normal mortals are unable to see. In Changelings case it just so happens that this exceptional quality in their souls allows them to nearly constantly see things that others may not. Remember that just like Mages, Demons or Garou Changelings are unable to remember anything past their current mortal life without a specific background that allows such memory.<br /> The Sidhe differ only slightly here. They are Fae souls clothed in flesh and have sent their bodies previous occupants away into the Dreaming yet like exactly like Demons they still have mortal memories and without that certain background do not really remember anything past those mortal memories. The Mists are a harsh mistress indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=104887#post104887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the mortal aspect of Changelings is barely addressed. That pretty sidhe princess was someone's little girl and that &quot;noble&quot; spirit inside her just smashed that child's soul, dreams and all and took over her body. And I find that hard to reconcile, because the game wouldn't really be the same if it was dealt with (too much like Vampire or Demon), but that fact it's not dealt with just irritates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling is all about balancing the Mortal and the Immortal sides of your soul and finding away to equally stand in both worlds. So that said I have no idea where you get the idea that the mortal side is barely addressed. Remember that your mortal family, and mortal authorities, do not just forget about you after your Chrysalis. If you disappear to live amongst the other Changelings exclusively someone is going to come looking for you, and escaping into the Dreaming or hiding in Freeholds will only drive you mad just as trying to exclusively exist within the mortal realm will slowly drown you in Banality thus destroying a part of your soul. And I must note that the Sidhe has not smashed that child's soul but sent it into the Dreaming, whether this is better or worse fate for the soul is something that can be argued either way as none, even the Sidhe, do not know or remember where those souls exactly go or what fate awaits them there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=104887#post104887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Lost really does accomplish something special that Dreaming just doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really must disagree. I like Lost quite a bit, I love the magic system and the Oath system there. And I am fond of the fact that in it the Changeligns truly are Fae beings who disguise themselves as humans through the Mask, although they used to be men once. And I love the Gentry there. Still I think the two games are quite different and thus not really comparable. Lost has one big weakness though, it's protagonists are always victims of abuse which can be a tough spot for some people, while Dreamings protagonists can be just about anything. Dreamings weakness in my opinion is in it's mechanics more than it's world. I do hope this is somehow addressed in the C20 without loosing that which makes CtD the game it is.<br /> <br /> Ctl and CtD are still both excellent games, as if DA:Fae as well but they are all quite different and about different things. A place for everything and everything in its place, you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:58:24-07:00","id":105807,"title":"","content":"If you think Changeling: the Dreaming missed some mark, that's fine. There are other games out there, feel free to play them. Changeling: the Dreaming, as it was, holds a special place in a lot of fan's hearts. If they fuck it all up for the people who already like it, to try to appeal to a bunch of people who <i>don't</i>, that would be the absolute apex of conceivable failure on one of these anniversary products.<br /> <br /> If a 20th Anniversary edition does indeed happen, I expect changes to be limited to cleanup and clarification only, without damaging the existing narrative style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:59:24-07:00","id":105886,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I thought PookaKnight said that it was a merging of essences that was not anything like what I described. But you don't seem to be on the same page with that. <br /> <br /> Sent them away into the Dreaming sounds so nice.... when you are ripping an unwilling person's soul out of their body and consigning it to what is pretty much described as a Hell of nightmares ruled over by evils so ancient they predate the Fae. What the sidhe did (and ALL the thallain too) was as or more horrible than any embrace. Commoners are no better. They did it a long time ago and do it again with every generation. That kid should have a human soul and the fae spirit either ousts it or merges with it without consent. <br /> <br /> I think it's barely addressed because it is basically barely addressed. Once you're a fae, the best your mortal life seems to be is a cover you are going to have to dodge ASAP. Because the banality of the world will eat you alive if you don't go live in a freehold. The game may be about trying to balance your Fae existence between Bedlam and Banality and the fact you are going to probably lose, but you WILL lose if you keep your mortal life. I have never seen someone persist in their job as a doctor or student or anything for very long. <br /> <br /> As for all Changelings, within the context of the game itself, they think what they are doing, but that's like asking anyone who profits from a bad situation about it. For another view on how Changelings might appear, look up the stuff in Hunter about them. <br /> <br /> BUT all that aside, I think the major failing of Changeling is that they aren't. Changelings that is. They are fae. There really aren't any changelings in changeling. Enchanted, I guess? <br /> <br /> As I have said, I have played it and enjoyed it and run it and enjoyed it but there is something about it that nags at me more than any of the the other lines (except Werewolf). It just doesn't seem to fit into the WoD the same way the other games do and stay true to both the source ideas and to the idea of personal horror that is central to all the other lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T16:09:20-07:00","id":105891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=105807#post105807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think Changeling: the Dreaming missed some mark, that's fine. There are other games out there, feel free to play them. Changeling: the Dreaming, as it was, holds a special place in a lot of fan's hearts. If they fuck it all up for the people who already like it, to try to appeal to a bunch of people who <i>don't</i>, that would be the absolute apex of conceivable failure on one of these anniversary products.<br /> <br /> If a 20th Anniversary edition does indeed happen, I expect changes to be limited to cleanup and clarification only, without damaging the existing narrative style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't disagree with you on any particular point. I think there should be a C20. I want there to be a C20. And not just because I want there to be a Hunter 20 or a Demon 20. I want it for itself.<br /> <br /> I just want to be able to say my piece about what some of my issues are with it. I'd be glad to do the same about Werewolf and I have much stronger feelings on that, but I would NEVER want there not to have been a W20.<br /> <br /> I don't want the core things that people loved bent and twisted out of recognition either. That being said, sometimes the stuff that they came up with in the NWoD was cool stuff and needs to be looked at. For example, Rotes MATTER in Mage the Awakening, they are pretty damn useless in Mage the Ascension. Mage the Awakening uses Gnosis + Sphere and Mage the Ascension uses just Arete. Satyr asked for input on why people wanted it one way or the other after stating where he is coming from.<br /> <br /> So, if I bring up the burr that itches me about the game, it's just trying to figure out if there's a way around it. Perhaps in some supplement I didn't read, haven't read or don't remember these things were addressed? I dunno. I'm a big afficianado of the mythic sources of the game. If it doesn't, maybe there is some way it can? I think it would say a lot about a sidhe to know how they feel about what they did to an innocent person (probably the kind of person the sidhe would want to have hanging around) to regain a foothold in the world. Deniers wouldn't think about it at all. Jerks would be totally okay with it. And some would angst over it. Those would probably be the good ones. <br /> <br /> Would you want me to throw my money behind a C20 Kickstarter? Or just go off and play other games?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:46:43-07:00","id":105933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=105891#post105891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you want me to throw my money behind a C20 Kickstarter? Or just go off and play other games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I made it pretty clear what I think you should do with your money. You had a chance to look at Changeling, and judging by your talk about soul parasites, you didn't take it. If there's a new audience to be drawn in by a more polished revision, it will be drawn from people who haven't invented flaws to be angry about that aren't supported in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T20:09:47-07:00","id":105996,"title":"","content":"Yep; people are passionate about the game.<br /> <br /> Ajax: to the extent that \u201csoul-stealing\u201d exists in CtD, it is limited <i>specifically</i> to the Sidhe, and is handled not unlike the fae abductions at the heart of CtL \u2014 except that the Sidhe are more sympathetic versions of CtL\u2019s fetches. One of the last supplements of the line even provides a rough analogue for CtL\u2019s changelings themselves: the mortals who were abducted to allow the Sidhe to return come back with a vengeance, changed by their experience in Arcadia. <br /> <br /> Oddly, CtD\u2019s commoners also have a rough counterpart in CtL: Charlatans \u2014 fae trapped in the mortal world and looking for a way to go home. The differences are two-fold: first, Charlatans are wholly fae; CtD\u2019s commoners are human/fae hybrids in much the same way that werewolves are human/spirit hybrids: they were born that way, but didn\u2019t realize it until their Chrysalis, when they awakened to their fae nature. <br /> <br /> Really, CtL and CtD are very much flip sides of the same coin. This is most apparent when you compare Banality to Clarity: in both cases, the high end pushes you toward the mortal side of your being, while the low end pushes you toward the fae side. The difference lies in how each game portrays those extremes: CtL portrays the human side as a good thing (e.g., sane, humane, and creative) while the fae side is something to avoid; CtD portrays the human end as, well, banal, and the fae side, while not precisely <i>good</i>, generally came across as the less dangerous of the two. <br /> <br /> The above illustrates how I think a Changeling Translation Guide should be done. It also illustrates the folly of trying to incorporate thematic elements of Lost into the official Dreaming game: they are thematically about as polar opposite as you can get while still talking about the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T21:21:59-07:00","id":106027,"title":"","content":"V20 felt like it took a lot of stuff from old editions and stripped out the things they wanted, and then stuck what they chose back into the book.<br /> W20 had a bit more finessing, but it still felt much more like &quot;we updated some stuff, tweaked some rules, but it's pretty much copy/pasted from what we found.&quot;<br /> M20 has apparently been completely re-written. Things were &quot;taken&quot; from other books, but more like the essence of those things were looked at and something new that represented it all was created.<br /> To be honest, I don't know Wraith, so I can't say if the Wr20 stuff is more like Apocalypse, or Ascension.<br /> Changeling only had 2 editions, so either they only have to amalgamate two editions into one with some updates for 2015, or to take the essence of what is/was C:tD and tweak it and write it to emphasize and present it in a way that keeps the game the same as it was for those who love/d it, as well and introducing new people to a game that fits a contemporary idea of &quot;fae&quot; now that Modern Fantasy is a &quot;thing&quot;. I don't think that C20 should be re-envisioned, or re-designed... but I think that casting lights in new areas and presenting it a bit differently could help make it appeal to more folks as I think that its reputation was created by those who had different expectations than what the game actually was intended to be about.<br /> <br /> I think that we'll have to see who Rich chooses to be the line developer, and what their vision for the book/game line is. If this book is going to be announced at Gen Con, chances are, Rich is already talking to folks and laying the groundwork... if he finds someone who he trusts and who's super-eager to take the C:tD ball and run with it like Satyr, then I think it could be amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:49:34-07:00","id":106301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=105996#post105996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep; people are passionate about the game.<br /> <br /> Ajax: to the extent that \u201csoul-stealing\u201d exists in CtD, it is limited <i>specifically</i> to the Sidhe, and is handled not unlike the fae abductions at the heart of CtL \u2014 except that the Sidhe are more sympathetic versions of CtL\u2019s fetches. One of the last supplements of the line even provides a rough analogue for CtL\u2019s changelings themselves: the mortals who were abducted to allow the Sidhe to return come back with a vengeance, changed by their experience in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Oddly, CtD\u2019s commoners also have a rough counterpart in CtL: Charlatans \u2014 fae trapped in the mortal world and looking for a way to go home. The differences are two-fold: first, Charlatans are wholly fae; CtD\u2019s commoners are human/fae hybrids in much the same way that werewolves are human/spirit hybrids: they were born that way, but didn\u2019t realize it until their Chrysalis, when they awakened to their fae nature.<br /> <br /> Really, CtL and CtD are very much flip sides of the same coin. This is most apparent when you compare Banality to Clarity: in both cases, the high end pushes you toward the mortal side of your being, while the low end pushes you toward the fae side. The difference lies in how each game portrays those extremes: CtL portrays the human side as a good thing (e.g., sane, humane, and creative) while the fae side is something to avoid; CtD portrays the human end as, well, banal, and the fae side, while not precisely <i>good</i>, generally came across as the less dangerous of the two.<br /> <br /> The above illustrates how I think a Changeling Translation Guide should be done. It also illustrates the folly of trying to incorporate thematic elements of Lost into the official Dreaming game: they are thematically about as polar opposite as you can get while still talking about the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the whole - Agreed. <br /> <br /> Agreed. Agreed. Agreed.<br /> <br /> That 180 degree polarization is part of my point. Beautifully said. <br /> <br /> That being said, I still think the noble and good sidhe (until the jerky Houses come along later, mixed with noble and good and noble and misunderstood) can easily be seen as soul-destroying monsters. Hunter takes this tact (for obvious reasons) and, when you read it, it's really compelling. I do remember them dealing with it, very late and kinda half-assed. Even then I thought, &quot;This is really a game-changer. Why hasn't it been dealt with before? Good guy sidhe having to come to terms with WHAT THEY DID to come back to world. How delicious! How often do they go Unseelie in self-justification? What about the potential for angsting to put them in danger of Banality? Bedlam?&quot; But it was too late in may ways. Too far along and the game was out of steam. <br /> <br /> Commoners are another issue. Sure they can be seen as hybrid beings, but they also come across as NOT hybrids, since the human part never really got to be human at all. They could just as easily be seen as non-human cuckoos who insert their otherworldly souls into the bodies of the unborn.<br /> <br /> Those are horrifying things. In the World of Darkness, that seems like something interesting to look into. Moreso, to me, than just dealing with the same category of issue in the &quot;how do integrate my abhorence of iron and my hatred of all the banal things that consitute MOST of modern life into the fact I still need to hold down a job to have a place to live and eat.&quot; I want to deal with THAT too, but I don't see why we can't have both.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:53:58-07:00","id":106305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=105933#post105933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I made it pretty clear what I think you should do with your money. You had a chance to look at Changeling, and judging by your talk about soul parasites, you didn't take it. If there's a new audience to be drawn in by a more polished revision, it will be drawn from people who haven't invented flaws to be angry about that aren't supported in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bought and read almost every supplement. Have used them to run several Changeling games and many mini-games.<br /> <br /> I CAN have an opinion and it doesn't have to agree with yours. I CAN want to see something different and more in Changeling when it comes out. I CAN think the game was flawed and suggest fixes.<br /> <br /> I am totally happy with them not being put in place. I can do it myself, give the game a pass, see if the update brings in more and different things and/or clears this away and pour my heart and soul into it, whatever.<br /> <br /> But I am going to talk about what I want and like. Hope that's okay.<br /> <br /> Thanks, Dreamweaver and others, for talking back and not just trying to shut me down and force me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-05-2014, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:02:19-07:00","id":106547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=106301#post106301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are horrifying things. In the World of Darkness, that seems like something interesting to look into. Moreso, to me, than just dealing with the same category of issue in the &quot;how do integrate my abhorence of iron and my hatred of all the banal things that consitute MOST of modern life into the fact I still need to hold down a job to have a place to live and eat.&quot; I want to deal with THAT too, but I don't see why we can't have both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question here isn\u2019t what <i>can</i> be done with <b>CtD</b> by individual Storytellers, but rather what <i>ought</i> to be done with it by the C20 developers. The notion of the fae as predators is a <b>Lost</b> thing far more than it\u2019s a <b>Dreamng</b> thing; and in a Translation Guide, it\u2019s <i>entirely</i> appropriate to suggest ways to integrate such elements of <b>Lost</b> into <b>Dreaming</b>. But that\u2019s not something that I\u2019d want C20 to play up. <br /> <br /> Your reference to <b>Hunter</b> is an interesting one, and one that I recall reading. I <i>also</i> recall thinking \u201cwell, yeah; of <i>course</i> they\u2019d interpret it as a possession. But they\u2019ve got it wrong, which is why all their efforts to \u2018exorcise the possessing entity\u2019 either fail or kill the \u2018host\u2019\u201d'. In short, it didn\u2019t strike me as a novel and interesting way to play changelings; it struck me as a good way to illustrate the potential ignorance of Hunters. I would <i>not</i> want \u201cchangelings are alien entities who destroy human souls\u201d to be a significant part of C20, as it has serious potential to detract from <b>Dreaming</b>\u2019s themes. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:30:59-07:00","id":106608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=106547#post106547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your reference to <b>Hunter</b> is an interesting one, and one that I recall reading. I <i>also</i> recall thinking \u201cwell, yeah; of <i>course</i> they\u2019d interpret it as a possession. But they\u2019ve got it wrong, which is why all their efforts to \u2018exorcise the possessing entity\u2019 either fail or kill the \u2018host\u2019\u201d'. In short, it didn\u2019t strike me as a novel and interesting way to play changelings; it struck me as a good way to illustrate the potential ignorance of Hunters. I would <i>not</i> want \u201cchangelings are alien entities who destroy human souls\u201d to be a significant part of C20, as it has serious potential to detract from <b>Dreaming</b>\u2019s themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as it represents Hunters being wrong, it can also represent them being right...<br /> <br /> It makes things nightmarish, yes. And those are dreams right? I guess I come from a place where interacting with Faerie should be either beautiful and terrifying or hideous and terrifying. If you aren't terrified of walking in the realms of the Fae, it isn't because things aren't terrifying, it's because you don't get what's going on. Everything is meaningful but nothing is what it seems. Everything is powerful. There are rules, but, as soon as you think you get them, you find out you were wrong all along. <br /> <br /> Dealing with visceral uncertainty and personal horror doesn't seem like it detracts from those sort of themes. <br /> <br /> Obviously, there are other themes in play, and those are, once again obviously, very important to a lot of people. I just don't things in Changeling NOT being scary. If you laugh. It's more of the reaction to something you can't process any other way than because it's funny. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T17:29:44-07:00","id":106623,"title":"","content":"That much emphasis on the fae being inherently horrific and terrifying is more of a <b>Lost</b> thing than a <b>Dreaming</b> thing. Yes, there should be nightmares in the Dreaming; and yes, encounters with the fae <i>can</i> be terrifying; but the notion that <i>every changeling\u2019s very existence is the result of an atrocity</i> takes it too far. <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> isn\u2019t <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Demon</b>; it\u2019s more akin to <b>Mage</b>, tone-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:47:30-07:00","id":106652,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=106623#post106623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That much emphasis on the fae being inherently horrific and terrifying is more of a <b>Lost</b> thing than a <b>Dreaming</b> thing. Yes, there should be nightmares in the Dreaming; and yes, encounters with the fae <i>can</i> be terrifying; but the notion that <i>every changeling\u2019s very existence is the result of an atrocity</i> takes it too far. <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> isn\u2019t <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Demon</b>; it\u2019s more akin to <b>Mage</b>, tone-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you say:<br /> <br /> Jim Henson = <b>Dreaming</b><br /> Guillermo del Toro = <b>Lost</b><br /> <br /> ? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:13:24-07:00","id":106660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=106652#post106652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Would you say:<br /> <br /> Jim Henson = <b>Dreaming</b><br /> Guillermo del Toro = <b>Lost</b><br /> <br /> ? </span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dreaming = Disney<br /> Lost = Grimm's Fairy Tales<br /> <br /> Apparently","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:41:55-07:00","id":106671,"title":"","content":"Wow; from <i>\u201cThanks, Dreamweaver and others, for talking back and not just trying to shut me down and force me out\u201d</i> to snide remarks in three posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:43:59-07:00","id":106673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/96439-is-there-any-hope-of-a-changeling-td-20th-or-at-least-a-c-td-c-tl-crossover?p=106652#post106652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><br /> <br /> Would you say:<br /> <br /> Jim Henson = <b>Dreaming</b><br /> Guillermo del Toro = <b>Lost</b><br /> <br /> ? </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Jim Henson did <i>The Dark Crystal</i>; so maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:48:42-07:00","id":106674,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I\u2019m with Dataweaver on this. Based on the story world, the art, the fiction, and the general tone of <i>Dreaming</i>, I think the emphasis is less on terrifying. I\u2019m only passingly familiar with Lost. It looks like it has some parallels to Dreaming, but it\u2019s a vastly different game, thematically. I used the Henson/del Toro analogy because that\u2019s what the Dreaming vs. Lost thing reminds me of: Labyrinth vs. Pan\u2019s Labyrinth. They're both good films, but they serve different niches. I don\u2019t want Sarah or Toby dying, and I don\u2019t want David Bowie to start dancing with the Pale Man. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}